    "title": "Washington Co. firefighter arrested on child molestation charges - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Mike Lepp No media credit provided. ,\n10 hours ago\nWASHINGTON COUNTY, Ga. (WJBF) – A Washington County firefighter is behind bars on child molestation charges.\nThe Washington County Sherriff’s Office tells us that 23-year-old Evan Carroll Chambers is charged with Rape, two counts of Aggravated Child Molestation, and Enticing a Child for Indecent Purposes.\nSheriff Joel Cochran tells us the alleged incident occurred sometime between April and July 2023, and was reported to authorities in March of 2026.\nNewsChannel 6 has reached out to the Fire Department regarding his employment status, but have not heard back.\nCount on NewsChannel 6 for more details in this case…\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WJBF.\n2",
    "summary": "The Washington County Sherriff’s Office tells us that 23-year-old Evan Carroll Chambers is charged with Rape, two counts of Aggravated Child Molestation, and Enticing a Child for Indecent Purposes. Sheriff Joel Cochran tells us the alleged incident occurred sometime between April and July 2023, and was reported to authorities in March of 2026. NewsChannel 6 has reached out to the Fire Department regarding his employment status, but have not heard back. Count on NewsChannel 6 for more details in this case… Copyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved.",
